{"id": "6ab0e488-59b1-4612-ab69-58396d51b4c2", "slug": "auralis-2", "title": "Auralis", "description": "Auralis Ideas Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-staff-featured-2026-05-22\"\nname: \"Auralis\"\ndescription: \"Auralis Ideas Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#4ADEDE\"\n  secondary: \"#60F1AD\"\n  accent: \"#60F1AD\"\n  background: \"#030712\"\n  surface: \"#18181B\"\n  text-primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-secondary: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  border: \"#27272A\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Playfair Display\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# Auralis\nSource: Neuform staff featured templates. Author: Sourasith Phomhome (@madebysourasith). Views: 181; favorites: 13; remixes: 14.\nTags: background, animated, webgl, threejs, effect.\n## Overview\nAuralis Ideas Background Effect is designed for delivering a visual treatment or immersive background effect. Key features include atmospheric visuals, motion depth, and flexible presentation layering. It is suitable for visual-first pages, motion studies, and atmospheric hero treatments.\n\nA u ralis Work About Services Studio Insights Contact Us Ideas Become Living Interfaces We craft immersive digital experiences with motion, clarity, and visual depth. Start Project View Reel\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Ideas Become; Living Interfaces.\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #4ADEDE, secondary #60F1AD, accent #60F1AD, background #030712, surface #18181B, text-primary #FFFFFF. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Playfair Display for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nCards, buttons, badges, navigation, and repeated blocks should preserve the source geometry, border treatment, and hover feel.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Auralis</title>\n\n    <!-- Fonts -->\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400;1,500&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n    <!-- Tailwind CSS -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script>\n        tailwind.config = {\n            theme: {\n                extend: {\n                    fontFamily: {\n                        sans: ['Inter', 'sans-serif'],\n                        serif: ['Playfair Display', 'serif'],\n                    },\n                    colors: {\n                        brand: {\n                            cyan: '#4adede',\n                            mint: '#60f1ad',\n                            dark: '#030712'\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    </script>\n\n    <!-- Iconify -->\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n\n    <!-- GSAP & ScrollTrigger -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n\n    <!-- Three.js for WebGL Background -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r134/three.min.js\"></script>\n\n    <style>\n        body {\n            background-color: #000;\n            color: #fff;\n            overflow-x: hidden;\n            -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n            -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;\n        }\n\n        #webgl-container {\n            position: fixed;\n            top: 0;\n            left: 0;\n            width: 100vw;\n            height: 100vh;\n            z-index: -1;\n            pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        /* Utility for GSAP Masked Reveal */\n        .reveal-wrapper {\n            overflow: hidden;\n            display: inline-block;\n            vertical-align: top;\n            /* Negative margin to fix spacing issues caused by inline-block */\n            margin-right: -0.1em;\n            padding-right: 0.1em;\n        }\n\n        .reveal-inner {\n            display: inline-block;\n            transform: translateY(100%);\n            padding-bottom: 0.1em; /* Prevent descender clipping */\n        }\n\n        .gradient-text {\n            background: linear-gradient(to right, #4adede, #60f1ad);\n            -webkit-background-clip: text;\n            background-clip: text;\n            color: transparent;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body class=\"font-sans min-h-screen relative selection:bg-brand-mint selection:text-black\">\n\n    <!-- WebGL Background -->\n    <div id=\"webgl-container\"></div>\n\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <header class=\"fixed top-0 left-0 w-full z-50 flex justify-between items-center px-6 py-8 md:px-12 mix-blend-difference\">\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-lg md:text-xl font-normal tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-white hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity\">\n            A<span class=\"text-brand-cyan/80\">u</span>ralis\n        </a>\n\n        <nav class=\"hidden md:block\">\n            <ul class=\"flex items-center gap-10 text-sm text-gray-400 font-normal\">\n                <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\">Work</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\">About</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\">Services</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\">Studio</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"#\" class=\"hover:text-white transition-colors\">Insights</a></li>\n            </ul>\n        </nav>\n\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"group flex items-center gap-2 border border-white/20 rounded-full px-6 py-2.5 text-sm font-normal hover:bg-white hover:text-black transition-all duration-300\">\n            Contact Us\n            <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:arrow-right-up-linear\" class=\"text-base group-hover:translate-x-0.5 group-hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-transform\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></iconify-icon>\n        </a>\n    </header>\n\n    <!-- Hero Section -->\n    <main class=\"relative z-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center min-h-screen px-4 text-center pb-20 pt-32\">\n\n        <!-- Headlines -->\n        <div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto flex flex-col items-center gap-2 mb-8 hero-text-container\">\n            <h1 class=\"text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl font-normal tracking-tight text-white fade-up-element\">\n                Ideas Become\n            </h1>\n            <h2 id=\"living-interfaces\" class=\"text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl font-serif italic font-normal tracking-tight gradient-text pb-2\">\n                Living Interfaces\n            </h2>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Subheadline -->\n        <p class=\"text-gray-400 text-base md:text-lg lg:text-xl font-normal max-w-lg mb-12 fade-up-element leading-relaxed\">\n            We craft immersive digital experiences<br class=\"hidden md:block\">\n            with motion, clarity, and visual depth.\n        </p>\n\n        <!-- CTA Buttons -->\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center gap-4 sm:gap-6 fade-up-element\">\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"group flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-cyan to-brand-mint text-black px-8 py-3.5 rounded-full text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity w-full sm:w-auto\">\n                Start Project\n                <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:arrow-right-linear\" class=\"text-lg group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></iconify-icon>\n            </a>\n\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"group flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-brand-cyan/30 bg-black/20 backdrop-blur-sm text-white px-8 py-3.5 rounded-full text-sm font-normal hover:border-brand-cyan/60 hover:bg-white/5 transition-all w-full sm:w-auto\">\n                View Reel\n                <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:play-circle-linear\" class=\"text-lg group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></iconify-icon>\n            </a>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <!-- Scripts -->\n    <script>\n        // --- 1. GSAP Masked Reveal Animation ---\n        gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n        function setupTextReveal() {\n            const textElement = document.getElementById('living-interfaces');\n            const words = textElement.innerText.split(' ');\n            textElement.innerHTML = ''; // Clear original text\n\n            words.forEach(word => {\n                const wrapper = document.createElement('span');\n                wrapper.className = 'reveal-wrapper';\n\n                const inner = document.createElement('span');\n                inner.className = 'reveal-inner';\n                inner.innerText = word + '\\u00A0'; // Add non-breaking space\n\n                wrapper.appendChild(inner);\n                textElement.appendChild(wrapper);\n            });\n\n            // Timeline for coordinated hero animation\n            const tl = gsap.timeline({\n                scrollTrigger: {\n                    trigger: \".hero-text-container\",\n                    start: \"top 80%\",\n                    toggleActions: \"play none none none\"\n                }\n            });\n\n            // Fade up standard elements first\n            tl.fromTo(\".fade-up-element\",\n                { y: 30, opacity: 0 },\n                { y: 0, opacity: 1, duration: 1.2, stagger: 0.15, ease: \"power3.out\" }\n            );\n\n            // Staggered masked reveal for \"Living Interfaces\"\n            tl.to(\".reveal-inner\",\n                { y: \"0%\", duration: 1.2, stagger: 0.15, ease: \"power4.out\" },\n                \"-=1.2\" // Overlap with previous animation\n            );\n        }\n\n        // Initialize GSAP\n        document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", setupTextReveal);\n\n\n        // --- 2. Three.js WebGL Background Animation ---\n        function initWebGL() {\n            const container = document.getElementById('webgl-container');\n            const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n\n            const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(75, window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight, 0.1, 1000);\n            camera.position.z = 30;\n            camera.position.y = 10;\n\n            const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true, alpha: true });\n            renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n            renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2)); // Performance optimization\n            container.appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n\n            // Create a custom shader material to mimic the glowing flowing lines\n            const vertexShader = `\n                varying vec2 vUv;\n                varying float vElevation;\n                uniform float uTime;\n\n                void main() {\n                    vUv = uv;\n                    vec4 modelPosition = modelMatrix * vec4(position, 1.0);\n\n                    // Complex wave calculation combining multiple sines\n                    float elevation = sin(modelPosition.x * 0.1 + uTime * 0.5) * 4.0;\n                    elevation += sin(modelPosition.z * 0.15 - uTime * 0.3) * 3.0;\n                    elevation += sin(modelPosition.x * 0.3 + modelPosition.z * 0.2 + uTime) * 1.5;\n\n                    modelPosition.y += elevation;\n                    vElevation = elevation;\n\n                    vec4 viewPosition = viewMatrix * modelPosition;\n                    vec4 projectedPosition = projectionMatrix * viewPosition;\n                    gl_Position = projectedPosition;\n                }\n            `;\n\n            const fragmentShader = `\n                varying vec2 vUv;\n                varying float vElevation;\n\n                void main() {\n                    // Map elevation to color mixing\n                    float mixStrength = (vElevation + 8.5) / 17.0; // Normalize roughly 0 to 1\n                    mixStrength = clamp(mixStrength, 0.0, 1.0);\n\n                    // Colors based on reference image (Dark Blue to Cyan to Mint)\n                    vec3 colorDark = vec3(0.01, 0.1, 0.2); // Deep blue base\n                    vec3 colorCyan = vec3(0.29, 0.87, 0.87); // #4adede\n                    vec3 colorMint = vec3(0.37, 0.94, 0.67); // #60f1ad\n\n                    vec3 mixedColor = mix(colorDark, colorCyan, mixStrength * 1.5);\n                    mixedColor = mix(mixedColor, colorMint, smoothstep(0.6, 1.0, mixStrength));\n\n                    // Add glow effect based on peaks\n                    float alpha = smoothstep(-2.0, 5.0, vElevation) * 0.8;\n\n                    // Soften edges\n                    float edgeAlpha = sin(vUv.x * 3.1415) * sin(vUv.y * 3.1415);\n\n                    gl_FragColor = vec4(mixedColor, alpha * edgeAlpha);\n                }\n            `;\n\n            // High segment count for smooth curves\n            const geometry = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(150, 100, 150, 150);\n\n            // Rotate plane to lay flat\n            geometry.rotateX(-Math.PI * 0.5);\n\n            const material = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n                vertexShader: vertexShader,\n                fragmentShader: fragmentShader,\n                uniforms: {\n                    uTime: { value: 0 }\n                },\n                transparent: true,\n                blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending,\n                side: THREE.DoubleSide,\n                wireframe: true // Use wireframe to mimic the thin flowing lines in reference\n            });\n\n            const plane = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);\n            // Position slightly down and forward\n            plane.position.y = -15;\n            plane.position.z = -10;\n            scene.add(plane);\n\n            // Add a subtle particle system for the dust/stars effect in the image\n            const particlesGeometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n            const particlesCount = 700;\n            const posArray = new Float32Array(particlesCount * 3);\n\n            for(let i = 0; i < particlesCount * 3; i++) {\n                posArray[i] = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 100; // Spread across x, y, z\n            }\n            particlesGeometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(posArray, 3));\n\n            const particlesMaterial = new THREE.PointsMaterial({\n                size: 0.15,\n                color: 0x4adede,\n                transparent: true,\n                opacity: 0.4,\n                blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending\n            });\n\n            const particlesMesh = new THREE.Points(particlesGeometry, particlesMaterial);\n            scene.add(particlesMesh);\n\n            // Animation Loop\n            const clock = new THREE.Clock();\n\n            function animate() {\n                requestAnimationFrame(animate);\n\n                const elapsedTime = clock.getElapsedTime();\n\n                // Update shader time\n                material.uniforms.uTime.value = elapsedTime;\n\n                // Slowly rotate particles\n                particlesMesh.rotation.y = elapsedTime * 0.02;\n                particlesMesh.rotation.x = elapsedTime * 0.01;\n\n                // Gentle camera sway\n                camera.position.x = Math.sin(elapsedTime * 0.2) * 2;\n                camera.lookAt(scene.position);\n\n                renderer.render(scene, camera);\n            }\n\n            animate();\n\n            // Handle Resize\n            window.addEventListener('resize', () => {\n                camera.aspect = window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight;\n                camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n                renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n                renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));\n            });\n        }\n\n        // Initialize WebGL\n        initWebGL();\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "auralis-2.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/staff-featured-2026-05-22/auralis-2.jpg", "source_name": "auralis-2-DESIGN.md", "views": 379, "forks": 26, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "5bd6211c-bd4c-467c-b442-4312cac4712c", "created_at": "2026-05-22T07:58:12.433844+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T10:47:06.936055+00:00"}